---
alwaysApply: true
---

CakeFlow Design System — mandatory

Use the shared CakeFlow design tokens and primitives.
Never hardcode palette colors in feature components.

Visual language:

- editorial minimalism
- monochrome only
- no accent colors
- no gradients
- no shadows
- no rounded cards
- no SaaS dashboard card grids
- hairline separators instead of boxed cards

Typography:

- Onest = UI/prose
- Archivo / Archivo Expanded = display/order number only
- JetBrains Mono = labels/data/dates/prices/IDs

Use semantic design tokens:

- page
- paper
- ink
- muted
- hairline
- tile

Spacing:

- Use shared `--spacing-layout` (16 → 24px), `--spacing-cluster` (8px), and `--spacing-nav` (16 → 32px).
- Do not add one-off gaps or max-widths in feature components.
- Spec label column is at least 78px and grows with the longest localized label.
- Authenticated shell width is `--container-app` / `frame`.

Controls:

- square corners
- square checkboxes
- ink primary button
- visible keyboard focus

If a design change conflicts with the CakeFlow design language, reject the generic shadcn/Tailwind default and preserve CakeFlow styling.

Responsive typography:

- Font-family roles never change by viewport.
- Typography sizes may adapt across desktop, tablet, and mobile.
- Use shared responsive typography tokens/utilities instead of one-off responsive font sizes.
- Prefer `clamp()` where appropriate for display text and headings.
- Keep body text comfortably readable on mobile; do not shrink it just to fit more content.

Localization:

- All user-facing strings must use next-intl messages in `src/i18n/messages/uk.json` and `en.json`.
- Supported locales are `uk` (default) and `en`.
- Do not hardcode user-facing copy in components.
- Do not translate user-entered bakery, catalog or order content.
- Format dates and times with `formatDateTime` / `useFormatter`, never a hardcoded locale.
- Follow `docs/i18n.md` when adding a new feature namespace.
